(1.5 0 0 -1.5 0 850)"></path></svg></a><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn" data-title="Show closest data on hover" data-attr="hovermode" data-val="closest" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="ne"><svg viewBox="0 0 1500 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="m375 725l0 0-375-375 375-374 0-1 1125 0 0 750-1125 0z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn active" data-title="Compare data on hover" data-attr="hovermode" data-val="x" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="ne"><svg viewBox="0 0 1125 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="m187 786l0 2-187-188 188-187 0 0 937 0 0 373-938 0z m0-499l0 1-187-188 188-188 0 0 937 0 0 376-938-1z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a></div><div class="modebar-group"><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn" data-title="Save plot as PNG" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="n"><svg viewBox="0 0 1000 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="m500 450c-83 0-150-67-150-150 0-83 67-150 150-150 83 0 150 67 150 150 0 83-67 150-150 150z m400 150h-120c-16 0-34 13-39 29l-31 93c-6 15-23 28-40 28h-340c-16 0-34-13-39-28l-31-94c-6-15-23-28-40-28h-120c-55 0-100-45-100-100v-450c0-55 45-100 100-100h800c55 0 100 45 100 100v450c0 55-45 100-100 100z m-400-550c-138 0-250 112-250 250 0 138 112 250 250 250 138 0 250-112 250-250 0-138-112-250-250-250z m365 380c-19 0-35-16-35-35 0-19 16-35 35-35 19 0 35 16 35 35 0 19-16 35-35 35z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn" data-title="Open in dialog (edit layout)" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="n"><svg viewBox="0 0 1000 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="M786 296v-267q0-15-11-26t-25-10h-214v214h-143v-214h-214q-15 0-25 10t-11 26v267q0 1 0 2t0 2l321 264 321-264q1-1 1-4z m124 39l-34-41q-5-5-12-6h-2q-7 0-12 3l-386 322-386-322q-7-4-13-4-7 2-12 7l-35 41q-4 5-3 13t6 12l401 334q18 15 42 15t43-15l136-114v109q0 8 5 13t13 5h107q8 0 13-5t5-13v-227l122-102q5-5 6-12t-4-13z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a></div></div></div><svg class="main-svg" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" width="694" height="494"><g class="hoverlayer"></g></svg></div></div></div></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(470,20)" x="470" y="20" title="codeHTML" width="560" height="419" class="codeHTML" name="codeHTML" rot="0"><foreignObject x="0" y="0" width="560" height="419" style="width: 560px; height: 419px;"><div name="htmlCode" style="zoom: 0.56; height: 748.214px; width: 1000px;" code="&lt;div class=&quot;ch&quot;&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Counter, D flip-flop and RC filter: bits and a bus in the wave viewer&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;ch-card&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Circuit Components&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clock (CK):&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;DigitalClock&lt;/em&gt;, 1 MHz, duty 0.5, first rising edge at 0.5 &amp;micro;s&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Counter (CN):&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;Counter&lt;/em&gt;, 3 bits: counts the rising edges of &lt;em&gt;clk&lt;/em&gt;; its outputs are the bus &lt;em&gt;s[0:2]&lt;/em&gt; (bit 0 = LSB)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flip-flop (F0):&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;DFF&lt;/em&gt; with D wired to its own inverted output &lt;em&gt;nq0&lt;/em&gt;: it toggles at every edge, so &lt;em&gt;q0&lt;/em&gt; is &lt;em&gt;clk&lt;/em&gt; divided by 2&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Filter (RC, CP):&lt;/strong&gt; 2 k&amp;Omega; and 0.5 nF on &lt;em&gt;q0&lt;/em&gt;, output &lt;em&gt;lp&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Netlist&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ch-formula&quot;&gt;
CK = DigitalClock(&quot;clk&quot;)&lt;br&gt;
CN = Counter(&quot;clk&quot;, [&quot;s0&quot;, &quot;s1&quot;, &quot;s2&quot;])&lt;br&gt;
F0 = DFF(&quot;nq0&quot;, &quot;clk&quot;, &quot;q0&quot;, &quot;nq0&quot;)&lt;br&gt;
RC = Resistor(&quot;q0&quot;, &quot;lp&quot;) &amp;nbsp; CP = Capacitor(&quot;lp&quot;, &quot;0&quot;)
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Digital outputs&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In the properties of the analysis, the rows &lt;em&gt;clk&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;q0&lt;/em&gt; (one bit each) and &lt;em&gt;count&lt;/em&gt; (the three bits &lt;em&gt;s0 s1 s2&lt;/em&gt;) are digital outputs, added with &lt;em&gt;Add output&lt;/em&gt; in &lt;em&gt;Y axe outputs&lt;/em&gt;. A bit is drawn as a step trace; a bus is drawn as a hexagon holding its value, in hex, bin or dec (&lt;em&gt;Format&lt;/em&gt;). The threshold between 0 and 1 is 2.5 V (&lt;em&gt;Logic threshold&lt;/em&gt;). &lt;em&gt;lp&lt;/em&gt; stays an analog output, drawn below. The value inside a narrow hexagon appears after a zoom.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;ch-grid&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ch-col blue&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Results (0 &amp;hellip; 20 &amp;micro;s)&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;count&lt;/em&gt; goes 0, 1, &amp;hellip; 7, 0 &amp;hellip; and changes at each rising edge (0.52 &amp;micro;s, 1.52 &amp;micro;s, &amp;hellip;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;q0&lt;/em&gt; toggles at each edge: period 2 &amp;micro;s&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;lp&lt;/em&gt; settles between 1.41 V and 3.59 V (RC = 1 &amp;micro;s, a triangle-like wave around 2.5 V)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ch-col green&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Things to try&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Change &lt;em&gt;Format&lt;/em&gt; of &lt;em&gt;count&lt;/em&gt; to &lt;em&gt;bin&lt;/em&gt; or &lt;em&gt;dec&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the threshold to a band such as &lt;em&gt;1,4&lt;/em&gt;: a value inside it is drawn red (unknown)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the counter size by renaming the bus (for example &lt;em&gt;s[0:3]&lt;/em&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
"> 
    <!-- Parent container that responds to mouse movement -->
    <div class="chtool"> 
        
        <!-- tool bar-->
        <div class="ch-page-toolbar" style="zoom: 1.78571;">
